    {
      "id": "decision:ADR-0003",
      "type": "decision",
      "title": "ADR-0003 \u2014 Simplify Folder Structure for Human Navigation",
      "source": "decisions/ADR-0003-simplify-folder-structure-for-human-navigation.md",
      "summary": "Use fewer, purpose-named folders for Echel's visible project memory and development controls.\n\nThe canonical structure is:\n\n- `wiki/knowledge`: concepts, systems, entities, flows, and standards\n- `wiki/decisions`: durable ADRs\n- `wiki/work`: task artifacts\n- `wiki/reports`: analysis, generated checks, and source summaries\n- `docs/development`: operating files for method, work, architecture, governance, automation, and evidence\n- `docs/development/state`: current state, resume snapshots, session history, decision log, and risks\n- `docs/development/bugs`: bug records and debugging evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "decision:ADR-0004",
      "type": "decision",
      "title": "ADR-0004 \u2014 Keep Product Wiki Outside Echel Core",
      "source": "decisions/ADR-0004-keep-product-wiki-outside-echel-core.md",
      "summary": "Generated projects keep `wiki/` at the target project repository root and place framework machinery inside `echel-core/`.\n\n`echel-core/project.echel` points `WIKI_ROOT` to `../wiki` so Echel tools can run from `echel-core/` while reading and writing product-owned memory."
    },
